R300: For v773 SpawnPosition, use the GlobalBlockPosition format: String dimension + Position (packed long) + float yaw + float pitch.
R301: For v772, reuse UpdateTagsPacketV771 because there are no tag changes.
R302: For v39 offline mode, set serverId to `"-"`, not an empty string.
R303: For protocol versions v28 and v29, still include the PreChunk (0x32) packet.
R304: For protocol v73, include the required S2C Entity Properties packet with generic.movementSpeed set to 0.10000000149011612.
R305: When configuring the end-to-end agent, set runMethodName to `d`, not `run`.
R306: When configuring the end-to-end agent, set serverHostFieldName to null.
R307: When sending Bedrock client-to-server packets in bot tests, use `sendPacketImmediately()` instead of the batched `sendPacket()` to ensure reliable delivery.
R308: Implement PrioritizedEvent<T> as a subclass of Event<T> that preserves the invoker() pattern and discards the plan's fire(Function, BiConsumer) method.
R309: Implement stop-on-cancel inside the invoker loop by iterating priorities from LOWEST to HIGHEST, breaking on FAIL, and then always running the MONITOR list while ignoring its return values.
R310: Migrate ServerEvents fully to PrioritizedEvent<T>.
R311: Keep existing .register(T) and .invoker() callers unchanged when migrating ServerEvents to PrioritizedEvent<T>.
R312: Have the Fabric bridge upcast PrioritizedEvent<T> to Event<T>.
R313: Provide a new register(EventPriority, T) overload for mods that want to register with priority.
R314: Make MONITOR listeners read cancelled state via a ThreadLocal set during dispatch.
R315: Use PrioritizedEvent<T> for all server-facing event definitions.
R316: Do not add adapters in the bridge layer.
R317: Do not create client-side stubs for rd-bridge-fabric.
R318: Do not create a separate rd-mod-loader-client module.
R319: Ship the rd-api client interfaces (DrawContext, ClientEvents, GameOverlay, KeyBinding, etc.) with a Fabric companion mod in rd-client that wires dispatch from RubyDungMixin hooks.
R320: Load client mods as Fabric mods via the actual Fabric Loader, not RDForward's ModLoader.
R321: For cross-platform mods, ship both rdmod.json for the server and fabric.mod.json for the client, either in the same JAR or separately.
R322: Keep rd-bridge-fabric server-only.
R323: Do not implement client hot-reload; leave it as Fabric's responsibility.
R324: Skip any task that touches a client mod loader or a client-side bridge.
R325: Implement client mods through real Fabric.
R326: Remove the existing static singletons wholesale: CommandRegistry (rd-server/api), Scheduler, ModConfig, PermissionManager, and the ServerEvents.clearAll() pattern.
R327: Replace those static singletons with rd-api interfaces plus a single implementation injected where needed.
R328: Rewrite all existing callers in RDServer.java to the new API in the same commits that remove the old API.
R329: Register built-in server commands (help, list, stop, tp, kick, ban, etc.) with the __server__ owner through the new CommandRegistry interface.
R330: Remove the Scheduler.init()/reset() lifecycle and make the scheduler a ModManager-owned instance lifecycled with the server.
R331: Leave existing feature classes (BanManager, BlockOwnerRegistry, GriefProtection, WhitelistManager, TeamManager, ServerProperties) in place because they are features, not API infrastructure.
R332: When rewriting any of the five API utilities (CommandRegistry, Scheduler, ModConfig, PermissionManager, ServerEvents), delete the old static class entirely.
R333: Migrate all callers in the same PR when rewriting any of those five API utilities.
R334: Do not leave static facade shims when rewriting the API utilities.
R335: Implement VersionCapability as a registry class with a static factory, not an enum, because enums cannot extend.
R336: Add an onPressed() callback method to the KeyBinding interface.
R337: Add an unregister(T) method to Event<T> for per-mod listener cleanup.
R338: Place ModDescriptorParser in rd-mod-loader, not rd-api.
R339: Before starting, clean the rd-api build dir of stale classes under the wrong package com.github.martinambrus.rdapi.* (Timer, Game, ModLoader stubs).
R340: On thread cleanup, interrupt the thread, join with a 5s timeout, and log a warning on timeout.
R341: Do not use Thread.stop(), which was removed in Java 21.
R342: Keep the old Event/EventResult classes in rd-protocol extending the new rd-api types for internal protocol callers, with rd-api as the authoritative API.
R343: Make the Core ModLoader scan only rdmod.{json,yml,toml}; leave plugin.yml and fabric.mod.json to their respective bridges.
R344: Implement tab completion on Alpha/Beta/pre-1.13 clients as server-side pseudo-only because there is no protocol support for Brigadier-style completion.
R345: Whenever a new memory is created in the auto-memory directory, write it in the corresponding `.claude/memory/` file in the repository.
R346: Whenever an existing memory is updated in the auto-memory directory, update the corresponding `.claude/memory/` file in the repository.
R347: The memory sync requirement applies to both `MEMORY.md` and all topic sub-files.
R348: Never delete world save files such as server-world.dat, server-players.dat, or similar without explicit user permission.
R349: Never reset world save files such as server-world.dat, server-players.dat, or similar without explicit user permission.
R350: Before any destructive file operation on non-code data files in the project root, always ask the user first.
R351: Every code change, whether adding a new protocol version, refactoring shared code, or fixing a bug, must preserve full compatibility with all previously supported clients.
R352: Backwards compatibility with previously supported clients takes precedence over clean code, performance, and new features.
R353: When adding support for new protocol versions, always test all previously supported versions after making changes.
R354: New protocol version support must not break older versions.
R355: Never assume adjacent protocol versions share the same format without verifying.
R356: When adding version thresholds, verify that all versions in the affected range behave the same way.
R357: When touching shared code paths such as packet dispatch, chunk sending, or login sequence, re-test at least one client from each supported version range.
R358: If a method is used by multiple protocol versions, never change its behavior globally.
R359: If a method is used by multiple protocol versions, add a version parameter and branch or create a version-specific override.
R360: Before editing any shared code, trace all callers to verify which clients are affected.
R361: Guard new behavior behind version checks so only the targeted client type is affected.
R362: Protocol adapters, registries, and version-specific code must be loaded and executed only when actually needed.
R363: Bedrock block palettes, MCPE servers, packet registry overlays, block state mappers, and translation tables should not be loaded at startup.
R364: Defer initialization of these lazy-loaded protocol components to the first client connection of that protocol type.
R365: Use JVM inner-class holders or synchronized lazy getters as appropriate for lazy loading.
R366: When multiple protocol versions share a handler method via cascading if-else chains on protocol version numbers, extract version-specific wire format logic into separate codec/strategy classes selected at connection time.
R367: Each session should only execute its own version's code path, never code for other versions.
R368: If only Alpha clients are connected, zero MCPE or Bedrock code should execute.
R369: If only 1.8 clients are connected, no 1.21-specific packet registry overlays should be loaded.
R370: Broadcast methods that write to sessions of mixed versions must dispatch on the recipient's codec, not the sender's.
R371: Follow `BedrockProtocolConstants`'s use of synchronized lazy getters as the reference pattern for lazy loading.
R372: Use `ProtocolDetectionHandler`'s dynamic per-connection Netty pipeline reconfiguration as the reference pattern for per-client protocol selection.
R373: Follow `BlockReplacementRegistry`'s per-version YAML delta shape: load each `/replacements/<protocolKey>.yml` the first time a coercion needs it, cache it, and record a missing resource as `NO_FILE` so the disk lookup never repeats.
R374: When a Bukkit/Paper plugin invokes a method on a bridge stub that has no real implementation, the stub must call `StubCallLog.logOnce(pluginId, signature)`.
R375: When adding or hand-tuning a bridge facade, keep the `StubCallLog.logOnce` call in any method that remains a no-op.
R376: Do not re-install the in-game broadcast sink without explicit instruction.
R377: If you get `BindException: Address already in use`, kill the old process first and wait 2-3 seconds.
R378: Whenever new functionality is added, test coverage is mandatory before the work is closed out.
R379: After the user confirms the feature works in their manual test, but before committing or moving to the next feature or task, audit whether tests exist for what was added.
R380: Both unit tests and integration tests are required.
R381: Do not add tests speculatively before the user confirms the feature works.
R382: Add tests once the behavior is locked in.
R383: If a feature genuinely cannot be tested at one of the two levels, state that explicitly to the user when reporting completion rather than skipping silently.
R384: Run the relevant test tasks to confirm the new tests pass before committing.
R385: Never run two Gradle test suites in parallel.
R386: Always run test tasks sequentially.
R387: Wait for one test task to complete before starting the next.
R388: Before launching any Gradle test, always check with `ps aux | grep -E "testCrossVersion|testLWJGL3|testModern|e2e-xv-|GradleWorker" | grep -v grep` to verify no other test is already running.
R389: If another test is already running, stop and ask the user before proceeding.
R390: Never run a full test suite when only a single test needs to verify a bug fix.
R391: Always find a way to run just the specific test in isolation, such as by creating a temporary focused test class, using `--tests` filtering, or adding a temporary include to the Gradle task.
R392: Delete any temporary test infrastructure after verification.
R393: Do not start tests proactively.
R394: Only run tests when the user explicitly asks.

